      "id": "claim_1218d607781245af879a1235cc9c9711",
      "statement": "A cell has the same states as a Durable Object: inactive (no node holds it — only a bucket object; every cell starts there), resident (in memory — active while working, idle while waiting), and hibernated (removed from memory with hibernatable WebSocket clients kept connected on its node); a cell keeps nothing across transitions, so the constructor runs again on the next event.",
