    {
      "id": "claim_c709be43d0c846d4aef28dfef02bea11",
      "statement": "The isolate pool is sans-IO: an isolate is not bound to a thread (v8::Locker installs the entering thread's per-isolate state so any worker can run a turn); what it is bound to is its JS state; two load quantities answer different questions — turns (queued+running, CPU demand for placement, counting the queue because an isolate serves one turn at a time) and requests (affiliated, memory demand, because a request's promise lives in the isolate heap so every later turn must come back).",
      "evidence": [
