    {
      "id": "claim_ce403be975af40e783b99eb9b92f96e7",
      "statement": "Alarm wake for inactive cells mirrors committed alarm state into the bucket as wake/<timestamp>/<cell> so a wake hint survives fence/crash/deploy; the system prefers a stale entry (one spurious wake) over a missing entry (a lost wake); boot-time orphan scan and a periodic waker tick list the whole wake/ prefix on the 5s sweep tick; alarms due sooner than the stay-resident threshold keep the cell resident when residency is cheaper than a wake cycle.",
